    <briefdescription>
<para>Approximate comparator struct template. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op" kindref="compound">binary_op</ref></computeroutput>, this struct compares two numbers with an explicit tolerance, given as a third operand: the comparison succeeds if the distance between the numbers is at most the tolerance (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ad3e5817bc88a8b60b769b39a5fefee94" kindref="member">detail::differ_by_at_most()</ref></computeroutput>). The result is computed at construction time. It is created by the <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-deprecated-literals_1gafe47800a219b00fcccf0a1dc596dbe20" kindref="member">approx</ref> (<ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1a27b015b0e2b40e0f0bbb1b08588e1c20" kindref="member">lhs</ref>, <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1ae1436f1b38c1062f7c733d3e8cb39b87" kindref="member">rhs</ref>, <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1approx__op_1ab1df01803852dcf0c603fda20a7e4f14" kindref="member">epsilon</ref>)</computeroutput> function comparator, and reported as <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1a27b015b0e2b40e0f0bbb1b08588e1c20" kindref="member">lhs</ref> ~ (<ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1binary__op_1ae1436f1b38c1062f7c733d3e8cb39b87" kindref="member">rhs</ref> +/- <ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1approx__op_1ab1df01803852dcf0c603fda20a7e4f14" kindref="member">epsilon</ref>)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The operands may be framework value wrappers or numeric literals, which are unwrapped; their own tolerance, if any, is not used.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Lhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored left-hand operand, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1ae9fe49cb0d38724533e9a27a2232bf09" kindref="member">stored_operand_t</ref></computeroutput>). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rhs_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored right-hand operand, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Epsilon_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the stored tolerance, either the operand type, or a <computeroutput>const</computeroutput> reference to it. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
